.TH MESH 1 "2026-07-07" "mesh 0.1.0" "MeshWatch"
.SH NAME
mesh \- control a MeshWatch mesh (meshd) from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mesh
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.RB [ \-H
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mesh
drives the same meshd HTTP API that the MeshWatch iPhone and Watch apps use: list
machines and their coding\-agent sessions, start a session running any CLI agent
(Claude Code, Codex, pi, or any command) with an optional natural\-language task,
read a session's output, send input, and read usage limits.
.PP
Output is human\-readable by default and machine\-readable with
.BR \-\-json ,
so agents can drive the mesh by parsing this manual or
.B mesh help
and then calling
.B mesh \-\-json.
.SH HOSTS
.TP
.B mesh hosts
List configured hosts with reachability.
.TP
.B mesh host add \fIname\fP \fIip\fP \fR[\fB\-\-port\fP \fIN\fP] [\fB\-\-token\fP \fIT\fP]\fR
Add or update a host. Port defaults to 8899; obtain a token by running \fBmesh pair\fP on that machine.
The first host added becomes the default.
.TP
.B mesh host rm \fIname\fP
Remove a host.
.TP
.B mesh host default \fIname\fP
Set the default host used when
.B \-H
is omitted.
.SH SESSIONS
Commands act on the default host unless
.B \-H \fIname\fP
is given.
.TP
.B mesh ls
List sessions/agents on the host (alias:
.BR agents ).
.TP
.B mesh peek \fIsession\fP \fR[\fB\-n\fP \fIlines\fP] [\fB\-\-pane\fP \fIP\fP]\fR
Print recent output from a session (aliases:
.BR output ", " logs ).
Default 40 lines.
.TP
.B mesh send \fIsession\fP \fItext...\fP
Type text into a session and press Enter. Quote multi\-word text.
.TP
.B mesh key \fIsession\fP \fIkey\fP
Send a single key:
.IR enter ", " ctrl\-c ", " ctrl\-d ", " up ", " down ", " left ", " right ", "
.IR tab ", " escape ", " backspace ", " delete ", " home ", " end ", "
.IR page\-up ", " page\-down .
.TP
.B mesh new \fIname\fP \fR[\fB\-\-cmd\fP \fIC\fP] [\fB\-\-cwd\fP \fIDIR\fP] [\fB\-\-task\fP \fI"..."\fP]\fR
Start a new session.
.B \-\-cmd
is any CLI (claude, codex, pi, a shell one\-liner); omit for a plain shell.
.B \-\-task
types a natural\-language prompt into the launched program after it starts.
.TP
.B mesh kill \fIsession\fP
Kill a session.
.SH STATUS
.TP
.B mesh usage
Usage/limits per provider (alias:
.BR limits ).
.TP
.B mesh health
Report whether meshd is up on the host.
.TP
.B mesh events \fR[\fB\-\-since\fP \fIISO\fP]\fR
Recent agent events.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-host \fIname\fP
Target host. Defaults to the config default, else localhost (127.0.0.1:8899).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable JSON output.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help;
.B mesh help \fIcommand\fP
for a specific command.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Add a machine and start Claude Code on a task:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mesh host add pi 100.101.102.103
mesh new fix\-bug \-H pi \-\-cmd claude \-\-task "fix the failing test"
mesh peek fix\-bug \-H pi \-n 60
mesh key fix\-bug enter \-H pi
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.mesh/hosts.json
Host configuration (name, ip, port, token).
.TP
.I ~/.mesh/token
Local meshd token, used when targeting localhost.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MESH_HOME
Override the config/prefix directory (default
.IR ~/.mesh ).
.TP
.B MESHD_TOKEN ", " MESHD_PORT
Override the token/port used for localhost.
.SH SEE ALSO
The MeshWatch installer:
.B install.sh \-\-help
.SH AUTHOR
Arya Teja Rudraraju.
